[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [DEBUG   ] [STEP 096] Project root: /Users/matthewsmawfield/www/Temporal Equivalence Principle/TEP-9
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [DEBUG   ] [STEP 096] Start time (UTC): 2026-09-21T15:11:03.515137+00:00
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096] 
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   TEP-9 step 096 -- Voyager SCLK clock-correction audit
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   The Voyager spacecraft clock (SCLK) is not free-running in the data
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   record: JPL maintains a SCLK -> ephemeris-time correlation file
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   (SCLKvSCET) that is re-fitted whenever ground calibration shows the
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   onboard oscillator has drifted.  Each NAIF SCLK kernel release folds
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   the full history of those calibrations into the SCLK01_COEFFICIENTS
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   triplets (SCLK ticks, TDB seconds, parallel rate in s per most
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   significant field unit).  The rate column is therefore the measured
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   onboard-oscillator rate relative to terrestrial time at every
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   calibration epoch -- i.e. the complete resync / re-rate history of
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   the mission clock, exactly the dataset expected if the onboard clock
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   ever had to be corrected against anomalous drift.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   Record classes
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   * fine calibration records: rate within 0.5 s of the dominant cruise
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   mode (2880 s per MSF unit); these are the measured-oscillator-rate
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   channel.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   * rate-mode records: recurring commanded rates (e.g. 2820.000x, the
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   47/48 programmed rate state) and the coarse early-mission records
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   of the pre-1992 reconstruction -- engineering states, not drift.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   * the 1979-03-05 Jupiter-encounter sequence is dense calibration
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   (~hourly records) and is retained but flagged.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   Physical framing for TEP
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   Under the conformal lapse A(phi) an onboard oscillator rescales with
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   local physics, but the calibration record bridges spacecraft-local
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   time to the terrestrial timescale: the measured rate is the *ratio*
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   of the onboard rate to the ground rate at that instant, so a lapse
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   contrast between the spacecraft's location and Earth appears
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   directly as a fractional rate offset (modulo light-path lapse
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   gradients folded into the DSN model).  The comet channel requires a
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   cumulative slip accumulated along a transit through the boundary
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   sector; the SCLK channel bounds the *instantaneous* onboard-vs-
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   ground lapse contrast along Voyager's trajectory.  These are
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   different observables of the same field -- the step computes the
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   bound and tests its correlation with the boundary crossings and
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   radius rather than claiming a detection or a falsification.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   Tests
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   1. Ageing-detrended residual distribution of the fine-calibration
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   rate record (quartz ageing is smooth; steps are the signal).
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   2. Crossing-window tests: mean |residual| within +/-90 d and +/-365 d
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   of the termination-shock and heliopause crossings vs the global
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   residual distribution.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   3. Radius trend: Spearman correlation of |residual| with
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   heliocentric radius (a sustained lapse gradient along the path
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   would imprint a radial trend; radius is degenerate with mission
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   epoch on the outbound trajectory and is reported with that
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   caveat).
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   4. Signed-offset step tests at each crossing: the channel-relevant
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   lapse signature -- a persistent signed rate offset after the
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   boundary -- tested by a step term in the rate fit and a
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   before/after window contrast.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   5. Trajectory geometry: angular separation of each spacecraft's
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   asymptote from the TNO axis and anti-axis -- the two spacecraft
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   sample different field directions (V1 near the mirror cap).
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   6. VG1 vs VG2 as independent clocks.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   7. Drift-interval channel (New Horizons control): the implied mean
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   oscillator drift rate within each calibration segment (phase
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   residual / segment length), reproducing the correction-interval
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   drift staircase of the earlier TVP spacecraft-clock study.  New
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   Horizons supplies the no-crossing interior baseline: launched
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   2006, still inside the heliosphere at ~60 AU, asymptote outside
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   both field caps.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   8. Journey-drift channel: every correction interval is placed on
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   the reconstructed trajectory -- heliocentric radius, ecliptic
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   position, speed, radial velocity, direction of travel relative
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   to the field axis, screening region (inner heliosphere /
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   heliosheath / VLISM), and distance to each giant-planet well.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   The TEP density-screening picture predicts the unscreened
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   lapse contrast should peak in the low-density heliosheath
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   shell and be suppressed inside planetary wells; the step
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   tests drift against each coordinate, contrasts regions
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   (with cadence-matched controls), audits planetary-encounter
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   windows, and integrates the cumulative proper-time wander.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   Radius, epoch, and velocity direction are mutually
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   degenerate on an outbound trajectory -- the correlations
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   are reported with that caveat and the cadence/epoch
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   sensitivity tests are run explicitly.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   Honesty notes encoded in the output
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   * SCLK coefficients are a JPL reconstruction (SCLKvSCET), not raw
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   oscillator counts; cadence is irregular (~monthly, sparser late).
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   * ppm-level deviations are dominated by ordinary oscillator physics;
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   the TEP statistic is correlation with crossings/radius, not the
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   deviations themselves.
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   * The measured bound |dnu| < ~5e-5 constrains the *instantaneous*
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   onboard-vs-ground lapse contrast; a cumulative comet slip of
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   ~1e-3 built up across a transit region is not excluded by this
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   channel unless the boundary is sharp *and* the oscillator couples
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   the same way orbital dynamics does -- a process-dependence the
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   TEP framework itself predicts may differ (electronic vs nuclear
[2026-09-21 15:11:03 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 096]   vs macroscopic-dynamical clocks).
